# Deep council, round 5: v5.1, the paired rule rewritten as you asked, and the one disputed point

## The v5 audits
- **Codex auditor (`narrow-d436/audit-v5-codex.md`): NOT SOUND.** The same point as v3: "do not infer priority from a total-and-part or supply-and-shortage
  shape". On everything else it was satisfied:
  - u3/clean-11 stays asked as the share;
  - none of the boundary cases is decided, with investment commitments "plausible overreach, not certain";
  - all six controls decline (u2/clean-10 "reasonable, with that ambiguity stated").
- **Claude-family auditor (`audit-v5-claude.md`): SOUND,** with two optional wording fixes, now taken in v5.1 (`edit.json`):
  - "one of these second sides of the same bet" makes the three shapes a closed set;
  - the example's sales become a steel mill's tonnes shipped.

## What is left: one question of scope, which is Alex's
- **Does D436 make the total, the volume or the demand the question for its three named shapes when the outcome names both sides without saying which is
  main?**
- His own words covered only the HBM shipments-and-shortage case: "算一个题"; option text "第二件事作为同一题的背景留着…都是同一个押注的不同侧面".
- The other two orientations are the recorder's Decided line. The PREREAD's main and second labels agree with all three.
- **Four Codex-family auditors** (v1, v2, v3, v5) read D436 as not licensing a shape-based choice. **Three Claude-family auditors** read it as licensing one
  for these three shapes.
- You (round 4) said not to require an explicit main label, because that "could reproduce the refusal".
- **My proposal:** put exactly this to Alex as one yes/no with the three pairs, since he is active. Plan the paired send on his "yes". On a "no", the
  passage is void and the line-4 class stays recorded against his ruling.

## The paired rule, rewritten per your round-4 points (`narrow-d436/paired_probe.py`, check passed on v5)
- **The source review decides.** Two blind reviewers read every written answer to a target or the share control, both arms mixed (`review-brief.md`). A
  material defect of kind (i), the wrong side asked, (ii) an invented measure, or (iii) the second side dropped, marked by both reviewers, fails the
  edited send. Kind (iv), the due day, is the separate D636 class: it is reported and does not decide.
- **Exercise** counts only "no ladder" from the frozen arm, not answers refused twice. It needs at least 6 of 12, spread over at least 3 of the 4 targets.
- **Controls:**
  - pool-9 and u1/clean-5 are dropped as entangled with D436; u1/clean-5 is one of the six theses put to Alex.
  - The six left are justified on their own grounds: two years ×2, no theme ×2, D417 ×1, no checkable date ×1.
  - The share-centred control u3/clean-11 is added: the edited arm must still ask the share, with no hard-line fault.
- **Budget:** one cap shared by both arms, $3.60, which covers the in-flight room ($1.18) plus both arms' expected $2.40. That is inside the ~$4.34 left of
  Alex's ~$6. There are 52 sends.

## Questions
1. Is v5.1 ready to send on Alex's "yes"?
2. Is the rewritten rule now right?
3. Is the scope question correctly his, and is it put to him correctly?

CONSENSUS or DISAGREE.

